  "body": "## Finding description and impact\n\nThe `Distributor` contract allows users to dispute a Merkle tree update by posting a bond (`disputeAmount`) in a `disputeToken`. If the dispute is valid, the Governor calls `resolveDispute(true)`, which refunds the bond to the disputer and reverts the tree.\n\n```solidity\nfunction resolveDispute(bool valid) external onlyGovernor {\n  if (disputer == address(0)) revert Errors.NoDispute();\n  if (valid) {\n    IERC20(disputeToken).safeTransfer(disputer, disputeAmount); // Reverts if disputer is blacklisted\n    _revokeTree();\n  } else {\n    IERC20(disputeToken).safeTransfer(msg.sender, disputeAmount);\n    endOfDisputePeriod = _endOfDisputePeriod(uint48(block.timestamp));\n  }\n  disputer = address(0);\n  emit DisputeResolved(valid);\n}\n```\n\nIf the `disputeToken` has a blacklist mechanism (e.g., USDC, USDT) and the `disputer` address is blacklisted during the dispute period, the `safeTransfer` call in the `valid` branch will revert.\n\nThis creates a dilemma where the Governor **cannot** resolve the dispute as `valid` (true), even if the Merkle tree is objectively incorrect. To unblock the system (clear the `disputer` variable), the Governor is **forced** to call `resolveDispute(false)`.\n\n**Impact:**\n\n1.  **Forced Falsification:** The Governor is forced to record a `DisputeResolved(false)` event on-chain for a valid dispute, breaking the trust and accuracy of the governance log.\n2.  **Unfair Confiscation:** The honest disputer loses their bond (`disputeAmount`), which is sent to the Governor instead of being returned.\n\n## Recommended mitigation steps\n\nUse a \"pull\" pattern for returning the dispute bond, or handle the transfer failure gracefully. So as not to make the system reliant on a Transfer going through.\n\n```diff\n    if (valid) {\n-       IERC20(disputeToken).safeTransfer(disputer, disputeAmount);\n+       try IERC20(disputeToken).safeTransfer(disputer, disputeAmount) {} catch {\n+           IERC20(disputeToken).safeTransfer(msg.sender, disputeAmount); // Send to Governor/Treasury to hold for manual return\n+       }\n        _revokeTree();\n    }\n```",
  "proof_of_concept": "```solidity\n// SPDX-License-Identifier: UNLICENSED\npragma solidity ^0.8.17;\n\nimport { Test } from \"forge-std/Test.sol\";\nimport { console } from \"forge-std/console.sol\";\nimport { Distributor, MerkleTree } from \"../../contracts/Distributor.sol\";\nimport { Fixture } from \"../Fixture.t.sol\";\nimport { IAccessControlManager } from \"../../contracts/interfaces/IAccessControlManager.sol\";\nimport { Errors } from \"../../contracts/utils/Errors.sol\";\n\ncontract DistributorPoC is Fixture {\n    Distributor public distributor;\n    Distributor public distributorImpl;\n\n    function setUp() public virtual override {\n        super.setUp();\n\n        distributorImpl = new Distributor();\n        distributor = Distributor(deployUUPS(address(distributorImpl), hex\"\"));\n        distributor.initialize(IAccessControlManager(address(accessControlManager)));\n\n        vm.startPrank(governor);\n        distributor.setDisputeAmount(1e18);\n        distributor.setDisputePeriod(1 days);\n        distributor.setDisputeToken(angle);\n        vm.stopPrank();\n\n        angle.mint(address(alice), 100e18);\n    }\n\n    function getRoot() public pure returns (bytes32) {\n        return keccak256(abi.encodePacked(\"MERKLE_ROOT\"));\n    }\n\n    function test_blacklisted_disputer_forces_wrong_verdict() public {\n        // Governor updates tree\n        vm.prank(governor);\n        distributor.updateTree(MerkleTree({ merkleRoot: getRoot(), ipfsHash: keccak256(\"IPFS_HASH\") }));\n\n        // Alice disputes the tree (Valid dispute scenario)\n        vm.startPrank(alice);\n        angle.approve(address(distributor), distributor.disputeAmount());\n        distributor.disputeTree(\"Valid reason\");\n        vm.stopPrank();\n\n        // let's make it revert explicitly to be sure\n        vm.mockCallRevert(\n            address(angle),\n            abi.encodeWithSelector(angle.transfer.selector, alice, distributor.disputeAmount()),\n            \"Blacklisted\"\n        );\n\n        vm.warp(distributor.endOfDisputePeriod() + 1);\n\n        // Governor tries to resolve as VALID (True)\n        // This should fail because it tries to refund Alice\n        vm.startPrank(governor);\n        vm.expectRevert(\"Blacklisted\");\n        distributor.resolveDispute(true);\n\n        // Governor is forced to resolve as INVALID (False) to unblock system\n        // This succeeds because funds go to Governor (msg.sender), not Alice\n        uint256 governorBalanceBefore = angle.balanceOf(governor);\n        distributor.resolveDispute(false);\n        uint256 governorBalanceAfter = angle.balanceOf(governor);\n\n        // Verify Alice lost funds and Governor got them\n        assertEq(governorBalanceAfter - governorBalanceBefore, distributor.disputeAmount(), \"Governor should receive the bond\");\n        assertEq(distributor.disputer(), address(0), \"Dispute should be cleared\");\n\n        // Governor can now revoke the tree manually since the dispute is 'resolved'\n        distributor.revokeTree();\n        (bytes32 merkleRoot, ) = distributor.tree();\n        (bytes32 lastMerkleRoot, ) = distributor.lastTree();\n        assertEq(merkleRoot, lastMerkleRoot, \"Tree should be reverted\");\n        \n        vm.stopPrank();\n    }\n}\n\n```",
